  "problem": "What is the minor of ${e}_{13}$ in the matrix\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & y \\\\ w-1 & 1-w & 3 \\\\ 1-w & w-1 & -10y\\end{aligned}]?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the first row and the third column:\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & \u2217 & y \\\\ w-1 & 1-w & \u2217 \\\\ 1-w & w-1 & \u2217\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}w-1 & 1-w \\\\ 1-w & w-1\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}w-1 & 1-w \\\\ 1-w & w-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(w-1)\\cdot (w-1)-(1-w)\\cdot (1-w) \\\\  & =(w-1)^{2}-(1-w)^{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
